+       <para>
+        Controls what happens when the planner stops flattening explicit
+        <literal>JOIN</literal> constructs because the resulting
+        <literal>FROM</literal>-list would exceed
+        <xref linkend="guc-join-collapse-limit"/>.  When set to
+        <literal>off</literal> (the default), this happens silently, as it
+        always has: the planner simply keeps the explicit join order beyond
+        that point.  When set to <literal>warn</literal>, a
+        <literal>WARNING</literal> is emitted naming the
+        <literal>FROM</literal> items involved.  When set to
+        <literal>error</literal>, an error is raised instead, preventing the
